title:    A 17-second outage that CloudWatch never recorded
subtitle: Per-second recording of the ALB target group, against the 1-minute metric the alarms read
width:    1180
---
# Recorded by scripts/run-experiment.sh, polling describe-target-health every 2s
 ELAPSED  FIS           HEALTHY  UNHEALTHY  FAST    TYPICAL
       0  initiating          4          0  OK      OK
       7  running             4          0  OK      OK
      14  running             4          0  OK      OK
      21  running             4          0  OK      OK
      28  running             2          2  OK      OK     <-- 2 tasks gone
      37  running             2          2  OK      OK
      45  running             4          0  OK      OK     <-- ECS has replaced them
      52  running             4          0  OK      OK

# The same window, as CloudWatch sampled it (HealthyHostCount, Minimum, 60s)
#   the alarms can only read this, not the trace above
  23:26   4.0
  23:27   4.0
  23:28   4.0      <-- the outage happened inside this minute
  23:29   4.0
  23:30   4.0

# ECS task records for the same event
  23:28:06   FIS issues StopTask
  23:28:45   replacement task running
  23:28:47   replacement task running
#            -> healed in 39-41 seconds

# And it is not deterministic. The 22:56 baseline run -- same fault, same
# service, same metric -- DID record a 2.0 for its minute. One outage seen,
# one outage missed.
